<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!--
  task3_fire_manual_1p6.xml - TEST VARIANT of task3_fire_manual.xml, as run in
  the practice pool on 2026-10-02 to tune the strafe hold. NOT the competition
  shot: the nozzle calibration (squirt_cal) is for 1.0 m.

  Differs from task3_fire_manual.xml only in:
    fire_range_m 1.6 (StrafeKeep + AwaitStrafeSolution)  the detector holds the
        whole face from 1.2-1.6 m; at 1.0 m it misses the windows (until it is
        retrained on close-range data)
    lateral_bias_m -0.10   aim 10 cm further RIGHT (by eye, 2026-10-02)
    num_attempts 1000, AwaitStrafeSolution timeout_s 1000000   no practical
        limit: the run lasts until the operator takes the boat back, so the
        gains can be tuned live (bt_runner_node strafe.*, docs/T3_running.md)

  The gains that held best that day were set LIVE, not here:
    strafe.kp_lat 100  kd_lat 200  ki_lat 10  kp_yaw 5  kd_yaw 0.5
    window_median_s 0.1  rate_window_s 0.5  ki_fwd 40  i_max_us 100
-->
<!--
  task3_fire_manual.xml - the fixed-nozzle shot in MANUAL, on the sticks: stand
  off the dock at the calibrated range, SQUARE to the face, SLIDE sideways
  until the upper-left window is on the nozzle's line, wait until the hull is
  still, fire. Repeat until the window goes out or 5 shots.

  WHY MANUAL. This hull is OmniX: it strafes. ArduRover's GUIDED does not use
  that (it turns and drives), so a sideways correction there means turning the
  whole boat - which moves the aim with every degree. In MANUAL the tree drives
  the sticks the way the team's dp_hold did (RC override: ch1 steer, ch3
  throttle, ch4 lateral), so the bow stays square and the boat slides.
  task3_fire_test.xml is the GUIDED version, kept for when GUIDED strafes.

  WHAT EACH AXIS USES:
    range (surge)      the LiDAR wall range, to fire_range_m
    left/right (sway)  the CAMERA: DockWindow x,y,z of window_index, in the
                       body frame - the window onto the nozzle's line
    square (yaw)       the CAMERA: the line through the face's two windows (or
                       the face plane), turned into a compass heading and held
                       on the compass between frames
  The LiDAR's wall angle is not used: the wall may not be flat, the face is.

  THE NUMBERS: fire_range_m 1.0 is squirt_cal on 2026-09-28 with the nozzle at
  30 deg (upper-left window; the lower-right wanted ~0.8 m, and the old 45 deg
  nozzle 3.22 m). min_range_m 0.6 so the floor sits below the firing range.
  Gains and the 120 us cap are dp_hold's tune on this hull. Re-calibrate on the
  real dock.

  HOW TO RUN IT. bt_runner_node with tree_file pointing here, the boat in
  MANUAL, then the SafePassage goal as for every tree. In the sim:
  tools/task3_sim/sim.py with its fire and fire-pump flags (its README).

  TWO SWITCHES, both off by default, both on bt_runner_node:
    publish_setpoints  may the tree take the STICKS (Gate G1)
    fire_pump          may it SQUIRT (Gate G7)
  With both off this tree is a shadow: it logs every stick command it would
  send ("strafe: range 3.41 m, window +0.12 m left ... [shadow ...]").

  TAKING IT BACK. telemetry_bridge forwards the sticks only in MANUAL, only on
  ch1/3/4, and releases them after 0.5 s of silence. So:
    SC out of MANUAL   the guard band ends the run, the bridge refuses and
                       releases the sticks: the boat is the pilot's at once
    SB                 the e-stop: motors off, whatever the software says
    (a drop switch on ch9, SD, when it exists, releases them too)
  The guard band also ends the run if the LiDAR loses the wall for a second
  or attitude goes stale; the runner then releases the sticks.
-->
<root BTCPP_format="4" main_tree_to_execute="FireManual">
  <BehaviorTree ID="FireManual">
    <ReactiveSequence name="guard_band">

      <ModeIs mode="MANUAL"/>
      <NotDropped/>
      <WallRangeAlive max_age_s="1.0"/>
      <AttitudeAlive max_age_s="0.5"/>

      <StrafeKeep fire_range_m="1.6" window_index="0" lateral_bias_m="-0.10" nozzle_y_m="0.0"
                  cam_timeout_s="0.5" face_timeout_s="3.0"
                  range_check_m="0" face_setback_m="0.0"
                  deadband_range_m="0.05" deadband_lat_m="0.04" deadband_yaw_deg="3.0"
                  kp_fwd="90" kd_fwd="60" kp_lat="90" kd_lat="30" kp_yaw="4" kd_yaw="3"
                  ki_fwd="20" ki_lat="30" i_max_us="80"
                  min_us="30" max_us="120" slew_us_s="200"
                  min_range_m="0.6" square_first_deg="10"/>

      <Sequence name="shots">
        <ForceSuccess>
          <RetryUntilSuccessful num_attempts="1000">
            <Sequence name="one_shot">
              <AwaitStrafeSolution fire_range_m="1.6" range_tol_m="0.06" lat_tol_m="0.05"
                                   yaw_tol_deg="5.0" hold_s="1.0" gap_s="2.0" timeout_s="1000000"/>
              <FireBurst burst_s="0.5" flight_s="0.8" ack_timeout_s="1.5"/>
              <!-- FAILURE until the window reads GREEN long enough, which
                   retries: line up, wait, fire again. With no lit window (the
                   pool) it just fires up to 5 times. -->
              <WindowOut/>
            </Sequence>
          </RetryUntilSuccessful>
        </ForceSuccess>
        <!-- Five timeouts and no burst is a failure, not a quiet success. -->
        <ShotsFired min="1"/>
      </Sequence>

    </ReactiveSequence>
  </BehaviorTree>
</root>
